<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peucetius</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peucetius is a figure of Greek legend, a son of the Arcadian king Lycaon, said to have led Arcadian settlers to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> with his brother Oenotrus. Ancient writers such as Dionysius of Halicarnassus used him to explain the name of the Peucetians of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, although that people's culture in fact grew from local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> communities.</p></div>
